{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349571068,"sessionID":"ses_f9e0f5af5ffeA69DAAPdxN5gxd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_92c82ec514f9487a9952ddc6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n2: \n3: This is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n4: `docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n5: \n6: - Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n7:   producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n8:   separate f32 buffer.\n9: - Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n10:   conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n11: - Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n12:   is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n13: - Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n14:   exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n15: - Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n16:   results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n17: - Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical\n18:   correctness, or performance.\n19: \n\n(End of file - total 19 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n\nThis is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n`docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n\n- Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n  producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n  separate f32 buffer.\n- Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n  conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n- Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n  is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n- Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n  exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n- Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n  results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n- Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical\n  correctness, or performance.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md","text":"# Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n\nThis is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n`docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n\n- Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n  producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n  separate f32 buffer.\n- Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n  conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n- Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n  is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n- Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n  exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n- Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n  results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n- Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical\n  correctness, or performance.\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":19,"totalLines":19,"truncated":false}},"title":